# Vivien, Arkbow Ranger, +1 with a target gone: Bot1 divides one counter each over its Llanowar Elves and Bot2's Elvish Mystic,
# then bolts the Mystic in response. The Mystic's counter is lost, not put on the Elves (the ruling, CR 608.2b), and only the Elves
# still gain trample. Turn 5: "up to two" allows no target at all (the ruling): nothing is put anywhere and the loyalty still
# rises, 5 then 6.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Vivien, Arkbow Ranger
Llanowar Elves
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Vivien, Arkbow Ranger.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Vivien, Arkbow Ranger.Activate(Ability: +1)
Bot1.Divide(Llanowar Elves: 1; Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic: 1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Keywords = Trample
? Bot2.Graveyard = Elvish Mystic
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Vivien, Arkbow Ranger.Activate(Ability: +1)
Bot1.Divide()
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Vivien, Arkbow Ranger.Counters.Loyalty = 6
